# Route from the Polestar route simulator's Horde consensus (Tauren export),
# visits 44-48, levels 45.9-47.6. Checked by lint, not play-tested on
# Forever yet. Era + known Forever quests only.
#
# Flow: Camp Mojache (where the previous guide ends) -> fly Gadgetzan
# (bind) -> Sandsorrow Watch -> Gadgetzan -> Caliph Scorpidsting -> Marvon
# Rivetseeker -> the Noxious Lair -> Dunemaul Compound -> Thistleshrub
# Valley -> Tooga's escort to Steamwheedle Port -> Gadgetzan -> Marvon ->
# Scrimshank's gear (OOX-17/TN if you found its beacon) -> hearth Gadgetzan
# -> (Hunters and Shamans: fly Orgrimmar to train; Druids: Thunder Bluff) ->
# fly Ratchet -> boat to Booty Bay -> fly Kargath -> the Grimesilt Dig
# Site -> Thorium Point (flight path) -> Velarok Windblade and the Cauldron
# -> the Slag Pit -> the lava spiders -> the Lookouts -> Thorium Point,
# where the next guide flies on to Stonard.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Tanaris: Sandsorrow Watch first, so Noxious Lair Investigation (82) is
#   in hand for the western loop; Marvon's Gahz'ridian ornaments are dug up
#   on that loop and handed in on the second trip south, with Scrimshank's
#   gear. Tooga is walked straight from Thistleshrub Valley to Steamwheedle
#   Port, where Screecher Spirits (3520) is handed in too.
# - The Blasted Lands pass (visit 45, Threat From the Sea) is gone: the
#   previous guide finishes that chain at Misty Reed Post.
# - The Badlands loop (visit 47) is dropped: a long ride from Kargath to
#   the far south-west for Broken Alliances (782, 3,600 XP) and to the far
#   north for Reclaimed Treasures (2342, no longer accepted on this route).
#   The Kargath bind and both hearths to Kargath go with it.
# - Caught! (4449) is taken, done and handed in on the way into the gorge
#   from Kargath, instead of being carried through the whole zone; Thorium
#   Point's flight path then replaces the hearth out.
# - Gadgetzan on arrival: Tran'rek and the poster beside the wind rider
#   master first, then Andi Lynn, the inn and Marin; Fizzledowser on the west
#   side last, on the way out.
#
# Optional: Find and Rescue OOX-17/TN! (351, 648): the beacon is a rare
# drop; the reward waits with Oglethorpe in Booty Bay. The Key to Freedom
# (4451): the key is a rare drop.
#
# Accepted here, finished later on the route: Sprinkle's Secret Ingredient
# (2641: the Violet Tragan grows in the Hinterlands), Rise of the Silithid
# (32, Orgrimmar around 50), Return to Apothecary Zinge (864, the Undercity
# around 52).
#
# Class training: Hunters and Shamans fly from Gadgetzan to Orgrimmar, and
# Druids to Thunder Bluff, at about 47, before Ratchet: the next training
# stop, in the Undercity, has no trainer for them. Everyone else trains in
# the Undercity in the next guide.
#
# Left out: Into the Field (243: no longer accepted on this route), Ledger
# from Tanaris (4450: the export never hands it in), Broken Alliances (782),
# see above.

step Marvon Rivetseeker
  tip West along the road south; Marvon camps by the ruins at the Broken Pillar. Put on his Gahz'ridian Detector: it shows the buried ornaments, here and around the Dunemaul Compound.
  accept 3161

step Broken Pillar: kill these as you meet them
  zone Tanaris
  tip South of the Noxious Lair the Dunemaul ogres hold their compound, with Gor'marok the Ravager at its eastern end. Dig up Gahz'ridian ornaments between the fights.
  collect 8443 quest 3161.1 @52.3,45.3 map 1446
  kill 5474 quest 5863.1
  kill 5472 quest 5863.2
  kill 12046 quest 5863.3 @41.5,57.8  -- Below ground

step The Noxious Lair
  tip West, the Centipaar insects swarm around their hives; any of them drops the parts.
  tip Careful: Centipaar Swarmers cast Silithid Swarm both in and out of combat, which brings small adds that interrupt you.
  collect 8587 quest 82.1

step Thistleshrub Valley: kill these as you meet them
  zone Tanaris
  tip West of the compound the cactus creatures fill the valley; only the Dew Collectors carry a dew gland. Most mobs in Tanaris can drop OOX-17/TN's distress beacon, rarely: keep it if you see one.
  tip Careful: The other thistleshrub mobs in the area are level 49-50 and wander a lot, so you can easily pull extra mobs.
  kill 5490 quest 3362.1
  collect 8623 optional                 -- OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon, a rare drop
  kill 5485 quest 3362.2
  collect 8428 quest 2605.1 @29.2,66.1

step Tooga's escort
  tip Tooga waits in the valley. Walk him all the way to his wife Torta in Steamwheedle Port, north-east across the desert: stay close, slow down for him and fight off what attacks him. Do not mount or hearth out of his reach. Yeh'kinya stands in the port too.
  accept 1560                           -- Tooga
  complete 1560 @66.58,25.67 map 1446 era

step Steamwheedle Port
  turnin 1560                           -- Torta, Steamwheedle Port
  turnin 3520                           -- Yeh'kinya

step Slake That Thirst
  tip Careful: Shadow Mages (level 42-43) call a Voidwalker while out of combat and attack with Immolate and Shadow Bolt. Thieves can Disarm you, Rogues move around in Sneak, and Assassins use Execute once you are at 20% health or less.
  collect 8483 quest 379.1 @60.0,23.4 map 1446

